uld push  her away and that he didn't necessarily  believe in himself but in the same  interview I mentioned above the director  of episode 4 gives a different  explanation when asked if Jaime was  slipping back into that deep bond he has  with Cersei David Nutter confirmed it in  the process he's saying that his  intention isn't to go and kill her even  if it means losing his own life but that  he really is still under her spell and  when you think about it this does  actually make sense  Cersei is the only thing he's ever known  well I imagine there's a good chance  that he'll change his mind once he gets  there it's fascinating to know that this  is actually his motivation it's as if he  found something better with Brienne but  doesn't believe that he deserves it and  that makes his character way more  compelling to me when I think about it  that way I do believe like I said that  he probably will change his tune when he  arrives there but let me know what you  guys think what do you think about all  these questions do you think Daenerys  will go mad Queen what did you think was  going on with Jaime when he left Brienne  how little Arya and the Hound do on  their trip to King's Landing and how  bummed are you that CGI is the real  reason that Jon didn't give ghost a  proper send-off when he left Winterfell  let me know in the comments please like  this video if you enjoyed it please  subscribe to my channel if you haven't  already to follow along to the end of  the season that's it for now thanks for  watching I will talk to you soon
 

